          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Super-Minkowski spacetime is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+spacetime"} super spacetime
            which is an analog in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            of ordinary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+space"} super Cartesian space
            whose odd coordinates form a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+spin+representation"} real spin representation
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Ordinary
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d+1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+space"} Minkowski space
            may be understood as the quotient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Iso
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Iso(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1})/(Spin(d-1,1))
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincare+group"} Poincare group
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            cover of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+group"} Lorentz group
            – the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/translation+group"} translation group
          %p
            Analogously, the for each real irreducible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            the
            = succeed "-extended" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim(N)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            %strong Minkowski superspace
            or
            %strong super Minkowski space
            is the quotient of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroups"} supergroups
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+group"} super Poincaré group
            by the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            (a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Klein+geometry"} super Klein geometry
          %p
            The
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-translation+group"} super-translation group
          %p
            Alternatively, regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            this is the quotient of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
            by the relevant
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+Lie+algebra"} Lorentz Lie algebra
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#CanonicalCoordinates Canonical coordinates
          %p
            We briefly review some basics of the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
            and the super
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+space"} super Minkowski space
            (see also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+space"} super Cartesian space
            and at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signs+in+supergeometry"} signs in supergeometry
          %p
            By the general discussion at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{Iso}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N})
            by its CE-algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{Iso}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N}))
            “of
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left-invariant+1-forms"} left-invariant 1-forms
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \mathbb{N}
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            be a real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(d-1,1)
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+representation"} Majorana representation
            for details.
          #CEAlgebraOfSuperPoincare.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℑ𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{Iso}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N}))
              is generated on
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e^a\}
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msup
                          %mi ω
                          %mrow
                            %mi a
                            %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\omega^{ a b}\}
                  of degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi even
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,even)
              %li
                %p
                  and elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\psi^\alpha\}
                  of degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi odd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,odd)
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in \{0,1, \cdots, d-1\}
              is a spacetime index, and where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              is an index ranging over a basis of the chosen
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+spinor"} Majorana spinor
              representation
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %p The CE-differential defined as follows
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{CE} \, \omega^{a b} = \omega^a{}_b \wedge \omega^{b c}
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 4
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mi ψ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{CE} \, \psi = \frac{1}{4} \omega^{ a b} \Gamma_{a b} \psi
                    \\,.
            %p
              (which is the differential for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product"} semidirect product
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} Poincaré Lie algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} acting
              on the given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+spinor"} Majorana spinor
              representation)
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi b
                    %mo +
                    %mover
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %mi ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{CE} \, e^{a }
                    \=
                    \\omega^a{}_b \wedge e^b + \overline{\psi} \wedge \Gamma^a \psi
            %p
              where on the right we have the spinor-to-vector pairing in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              (
              %a{:href => "Majorana+spinor#SpinorToVectorBilinearPairing"}> def.
              ).
            %p
              This defines the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+super+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré super Lie algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              this becomes the CE algebra of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+translation+algebra"} super translation algebra
              underlying super Minkowski spacetime.
          %p
            In this way the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super-Poincaré Lie algebra
            and its extensions is usefully discussed for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#DAuriaFre82"}> D’Auria-Fré 82
            ) and in (
            %a{:href => "AzcarragaTownsend89"}> Azcárraga-Townsend 89
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#CAIB99"} CAIB 99
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+space"} super Minkowski space
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The abstract generators in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CEAlgebraOfSuperPoincare"}
              are identified with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+invariant+1-forms"} left invariant 1-forms
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-translation+group"} super-translation group
              (= super Minkowski spacetime) as follows.
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+spin+representation"} real spin representation
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x^a, \theta^\alpha)
              be the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert N}
              underlying the super-Minkowski super translation group. Then the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vielbein"} super vielbein
              is the
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+differential+form"} super differential form
              with components
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi α
                        %mo ≔
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi d
                        %msup
                          %mi θ
                          %mi α
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi^\alpha \coloneqq \mathbf{d} \theta^\alpha
                  \.
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mi a
                        %mo ≔
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi d
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi a
                        %mo +
                        %mover
                          %mi θ
                          %mo ¯
                        %msup
                          %mi Γ
                          %mi a
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi d
                        %mi θ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^a \coloneqq \mathbf{d} x^a + \overline{\theta} \Gamma^a \mathbf{d} \theta
                  \.
            %p
              Notice that this then gives the above formula for the differential of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-vielbein"} super-vielbein
              in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CEAlgebraOfSuperPoincare"}
              as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                            %msup
                              %mi e
                              %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mi a
                            %mo +
                            %mfrac
                              %mi i
                              %mn 2
                            %mover
                              %mi θ
                              %mo ¯
                            %msup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                            %mi d
                            %mi θ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mfrac
                              %mi i
                              %mn 2
                            %mi d
                            %mover
                              %mi θ
                              %mo ¯
                            %msup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                            %mi d
                            %mi θ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mfrac
                              %mi i
                              %mn 2
                            %mover
                              %mi ψ
                              %mo ¯
                            %msup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                            %mi ψ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    d e^a &amp; = d (d x^a + \frac{i}{2} \overline{\theta} \Gamma^a d \theta)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = \frac{i}{2} d \overline{\theta}\Gamma^a d \theta
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = \frac{i}{2} \overline{\psi}\Gamma^a \psi
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          #Supertorsion.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The term
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %mi ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{i}{2}\bar \psi \Gamma^a \psi
              is sometimes called the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supertorsion"} supertorsion
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-vielbein"} super-vielbein
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi CE
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi a
                    %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %mi ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{CE} e^{a } -\omega^a{}_b \wedge e^b = \frac{i}{2}\bar \psi \Gamma^a \psi
            %p
              may be read as saying that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
              is
              = succeed "-free" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion"} torsion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔰𝔦𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{siso})
              which have “all indices contracted”. See also at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+constraints+in+supergravity"} torsion constraints in supergravity
            %p Notably we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mover
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo ∧
                      %msup
                        %mi Γ
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mi p
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mn 1
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mi p
                      %mo )
                    %mo ∝
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mover
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo ∧
                      %msup
                        %mi Γ
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi a
