            %p
              This shows that if
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GroupOperationOnSuperMinkowski"} (4)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+operation"} group product
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SuperManifolds"} SuperManifolds
              then the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
              is the super-Minkowski
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+translation+Lie+algebra"} super translation Lie algebra
              and hence that this group object is the desired super-Minkowski super Lie group.
            %p
              So, defining the remaining
              = succeed "-operations" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            %p
