            %p
              and indeed it does — the term
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi θ
                      %mo ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %mi θ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \big(\overline{\theta} \Gamma^a \theta\big)
              vanishes because the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta^\alpha
              anti-commute among themselves, while the pairing
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SpinorToVectorPairingForSuperMinkowski"} (1)
              is symmetric:
            %svg{:height => "205.898pt", :version => "1.2", :viewbox => "0 0 656.07 205.898", :width => "656.07pt", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
