          %h3#cohomology_and_super_branes
            Cohomology and super
            = succeed "-branes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p
            As opposed to ordinary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+space"} Minkowski space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+invariant+forms"} left invariant forms
            of super-Minkowski space contains nontrivial exceptional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycles"} cocycles
            (the
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wess-Zumino-Witten+model"} WZW terms
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
            (see there for more) of super-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            \-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            propagating on super-Minkowski space (
            %a{:href => "#FSS13"}> FSS 13
            ).
          %p
            The corresponding
            = succeed "-extensions" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+superspacetime"} extended superspacetime
          %h3#AsCentralExtensionOfTheSuperpoint As a central extension of the superpoint
          %p
            Regarded as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N}
            has the single nontrivial super-Lie bracket given by the spinor bilinear pairing
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ¯
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\overline{(-)}\Gamma (-)
                  \\colon
                  S \otimes S \longrightarrow V
          %p
            discussed in detail at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
          %p
            Notice that this means that if one regards the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi dim
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0|dim(N)}
            as an
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                abelian super Lie algebra
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/abelian+super+Lie+algebra"} ?
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+extension"} Lie algebra extension
            of that by this bilinear pairing regarded as a super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cocycle
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
